<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.16.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02034</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.16.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4fbbcbfc-c875-4601-8a9c-7d6f8f6d3a8d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><para id="para-00001">Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section id="sect-00002"><exercise id="_3bdda842-a202-4cfa-96bf-c80303719329" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00001"><para id="para-00002">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph that represents <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00001"><para id="para-00003">Correct! 2. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is found by using the squared term of the vertex form. The value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is 2.</para><para id="para-00004">Try again. Revisit activities 7.16.2 – 7.16.4.</para><para id="para-00005">The correct answer is 2. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is found by using the squared term of the vertex form. The value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is 2.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="b9a9a833-8d7c-4a05-be34-ce23d9a12115" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00002"><para id="para-00006">What is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph that represents <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00002"><para id="para-00007">Correct! -8. In vertex form, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is the constant. The value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -8.</para><para id="para-00008">Try again. Revisit activities 7.16.2 – 7.16.4.</para><para id="para-00009">The correct answer is -8. In vertex form, the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is the constant. The value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph is -8.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_10697901-1d71-4c1e-8aa3-341cded90fed" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00003"><para id="para-00010">Where is the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept for the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> located?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00003"><para id="para-00011">Correct! -4. Substitute 0 for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and you get <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para><para id="para-00012">Try again. Revisit activities 7.16.2 – 7.16.4.</para><para id="para-00013">The correct answer is -4. Substitute 0 for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and you get <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_7614b261-dbad-48ee-a025-2f05bc4aa041" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00004"><para id="para-00014">Which of the following is another point on the graph of the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      <para id="para-00015">Multiple Choice:</para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00004"><para id="para-00020">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is 2 horizontal units to the left of the vertical line containing the vertex (the axis of symmetry). Using the symmetry of the graph, another point with the same <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate is located 2 horizontal units to the right of the vertical line containing the vertex.</para><para id="para-00021">Try again. Revisit activity 7.16.2.</para><para id="para-00022">The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept is 2 horizontal units to the left of the vertical line containing the vertex (the axis of symmetry). Using the symmetry of the graph, another point with the same <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate is located 2 horizontal units to the right of the vertical line containing the vertex.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_51a7d19d-acae-4276-9c8c-dd6ad3831974" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00005"><para id="para-00023">Which graph is a representation of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00005"><para id="para-00024">Correct! Yes graph A.</para><para id="para-00025">Try again. Revisit activities 7.16.3 and 7.16.4.</para><para id="para-00026">The correct answer is Yes.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_57ca4658-384a-4e06-88db-22c107551c69" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00006"><para id="para-00027">Without graphing, determine if the vertex of the graph representing <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> shows the minimum or maximum value of the function.</para><para id="para-00028">The function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <para id="para-00029">Multiple Choice:</para><para id="para-00030">The vertex shows the minimum value.</para><para id="para-00031">The vertex shows the maximum value.</para></problem><solution id="sol-00006"><para id="para-00032">Correct! The vertex shows the minimum value. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value, or the coefficient of the squared term is positive, so the graph opens upward.This means the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is the minimum value of the function. The vertex is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. To verify your response, enter a couple of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> -values on either side of -5 into the function. For example, find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. Each time, the output is greater than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para><para id="para-00033">Try again. Revisit activity 7.14.2.</para><para id="para-00034">The correct answer is: The vertex shows the minimum value. The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>a</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-value, or the coefficient of the squared term is positive, so the graph opens upward.This means the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of the vertex is the minimum value of the function. The vertex is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. To verify your response, enter a couple of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> -values on either side of -5 into the function. For example, find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. Each time, the output is greater than <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>v</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_88f0ebcf-8946-42f3-9d92-5ccad7f2a77e" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00007"><para id="para-00035">Choose the equation that matches the graph of parabola D .</para>
      <para id="para-00036">Multiple Choice:</para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00007"><para id="para-00041">Correct! <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para id="para-00042">Try again. Revisit activity 7.16.3.</para><para id="para-00043">The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_7786bff1-c50b-4411-b3e8-1b0fcf3eded0" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00008"><para id="para-00044">Choose the equation that matches the graph B.</para>
      <para id="para-00045">Multiple Choice:</para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00008"><para id="para-00050">Try again. Revisit activity 7.16.3.
    </para><para id="para-00051">The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.
    </para></solution></exercise>
      
      <exercise id="_26117eea-4e73-4f7b-8e19-a0eecac697c2" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009"><para id="para-00052">Choose the equation that matches the graph C.</para>
      <para id="para-00053">Multiple Choice:</para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para><para><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></problem><solution id="sol-00009"><para id="para-00058">Try again. Revisit activity 7.16.3.</para><para id="para-00059">The correct answer is: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mi>−</m:mi><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
